  "description": "The PD4 does it all. Built using X6 series lightweight aluminum, the PD4 frame features a tapered internal headset and internal cable routing to keep a clean frame and its housing tucked away. Its 1x drive train provides a wide gear ratio, yet keeps things light and simple with no front derailleur and shifter to deal with. Lightweight and durable Weinmann U-28 alloy double wall rims are strong and built to last and matched to Kenda's Kwick Seven.5 tires with reflective sidewalls. On top of this, the PD4 features a Shimano 11-speed Deore XT Shadow rear derailleur and a RockShox Judy Silver suspension fork complete with a remote lockout that allows you to create a rigid fork on the fly, when needed.\nHaro PD4 27.5\" X6 alloy frame\nJudy Silver, 27.5\" Boost fork, 100mm, w/ remote Lockout\nFSA Comet Modular 34T crankset\nXT 11-spd Shadow rear derailleur\nSLX M7000 11-spd shifter & 11-46T cassette\nWTB Comfort Sport saddle\nWeinmann U-28 DW 27.5\" rims\nAlivio / Altus, Front T/A, 36h hubs\nShimano Mechanical BR-M375 disc brakes\nShimano BL-T4000 brake levers",
